# t3dev project configuration. Sourced by dev-up as shell.
#
# DEV_CMD        command that starts the dev server. "{{port}}" is replaced
#                with the port t3dev allocated. PORT and T3DEV_PORT are also
#                exported, so most tools need no {{port}} at all.
# DEV_READY_PATH path used by `t3dev-status --probe`.
#
# The command runs through a login shell (bash -lc) inside the worktree.

# wrangler ignores PORT and binds its own default, so the allocated port has
# to be passed explicitly or Caddy proxies to nothing. The console is built
# first because the Worker serves it from console/dist as static assets —
# `predev` only creates that directory, it does not fill it.
DEV_CMD="pnpm run console:build && pnpm dev --port {{port}}"
DEV_READY_PATH="/"
